  "title": "Outdoor Kitchen & Entryway Stone Ideas | June 2025 GenStone",
  "description": "See June 2025 GenStone outdoor kitchen and entryway projects. Get ideas for backyard upgrades and curb appeal improvements.",
  "canonicalUrl": "https://genstone.com/insights/project-spotlights/june-2025",
  "text": "GenStone Project Highlights – June 2025 Outdoor Kitchen & Entryway Projects\n\nAmanda Lombard\nDirector\n\nJune projects highlighted outdoor living and entry upgrades, with homeowners improving both backyard spaces and front entrances. These projects show how GenStone helps create a more finished, welcoming look inside and out.\nTry Visualizer Get Project Planning Guide\n\n\"We have had numerous neighbors stop and tell us that it looked beautiful. We couldn't be happier!\"\n\nRoclynn\n\nOutdoor Kitchen Projects\n\nExplore more outdoor kitchen stone ideas\n\nOutdoor kitchens continue to be a top project for summer. June featured grill surrounds, bar areas, and cooking spaces that brought together function and style. These projects show how GenStone can help define outdoor spaces and create a cohesive look.\n\n<iframe title=\"#MyGenStoneDIY - Keystone Bar &amp; Grill by Brent\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/767045735?dnt=1&amp;app_id=122963\" width=\"219\" height=\"390\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"></iframe> 40\n\nBrent’s Faux Stone BBQ Station\nLooking for a way to improve your grill? Take a look at this beautiful faux stone BBQ station project! The stone veneer brings it to life!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n30\n\nDanny’s Patio BBQ\nFeaturing a mini fridge, sink and full grilling station, Danny created kitchen on his patio with an outdoor kitchen kit and GenStone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nVanilla Bean\n\n1\n\nDaniel’s Stone Veneer Outdoor Kitchen Idea\nThinking of upgrading your outdoor kitchen? Check out this DIY outdoor kitchen idea that uses our Keystone stone veneer!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n2\n\nJamie’s DIY Stone BBQ Design\nCheck out Jamie's DIY BBQ grill area for design ideas and GenStone will help you find the perfect faux stone. Build your own stone BBQ area today!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n8\n\nJeff’s DIY Outdoor Kitchen Project\nPlanning a DIY outdoor kitchen project? Take a look at Jeff's incredible outdoor kitchen using our Desert Sunrise Stacked Stone!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n3\n\nLinda’s Stone Veneer for Outdoor Kitchen\nLinda chose to upgrade her outdoor space using GenStone's Desert Sunrise to complete this stone veneer for outdoor kitchen project.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\nRob Dean\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/9Geu6TAmBVcDskZfhGmnzP.jpg\" data-uuid=\"9Geu6TAmBVcDskZfhGmnzP\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 65\n\nOutdoor BBQ Island\nDIY Outdoor Grill Station, Stacked Stone Outdoor BBQ Island with Grill Station & Bar. GenStone can help you with Do it Yourself Outdoor Island ideas.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/PUxsegkTjU4YnNTHs5BN4e.jpg\" data-uuid=\"PUxsegkTjU4YnNTHs5BN4e\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 3\n\nRyan’s Faux Stone Grill Idea\nDo you have a grill or outdoor kitchen you need an upgrade idea for? Take a look at Ryan's grill idea that uses our faux stone!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n5\n\nWanda’s Easy DIY Outdoor Kitchen\nOur Keystone Stacked Stone panels made an easy DIY outdoor kitchen for the countertop next to the barbeque in this customer's yard.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n11\n\nTom’s Faux Stone DIY Grill\nLooking to give your BBQ a little something special? Take a look at this beautiful DIY grill project using our faux stone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nEntryway Projects\n\nView more front door stone ideas\n\nEntryways are one of the most visible parts of a home, making them a great place for a stone upgrade. June projects included front door surrounds and entry facades that created a stronger first impression and improved curb appeal.\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/PAErmxXAc7fWagnFkXdgMW.jpg\" data-uuid=\"PAErmxXAc7fWagnFkXdgMW\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 1\n\nJason’s Faux Stone Home Entry\nGenStone's faux stone panels transformed Jason's home entry with wainscoting and pillars. Take a look at the video of this project!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nVanilla Bean\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/MnJ4znjcuK9wieqxvCN4sM.jpg\" data-uuid=\"MnJ4znjcuK9wieqxvCN4sM\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/>\n\nMichael’s Faux Stone Garage And Entry\nOur faux stone is great at dressing up a home's garage and entry. Take a look at Michael's project for inspiration!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n6\n\nRobert’s DIY Faux Stone Entry\nLooking to change the appearance of your front door? Take a look at this DIY entry project using GenStone's Kenai faux stone!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n1193\n\nStephanie’s Stacked Stone Front Entry\nBeautiful entryway that frames the doors and gives a stark contrast to the paint and wood of the rest of the exterior.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nIron Ore\n\nEllie Peretz\nAssistant Manager\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/6Sv1fZm3i7QiNVat24dCZf.jpg\" data-uuid=\"6Sv1fZm3i7QiNVat24dCZf\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2\n\nSteve’s Faux Stone Home Entryway\nLooking for DIY inspiration for your home entry? Check out this beautiful home entryway project made using GenStone's faux stone!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nCoffee\n\n9\n\nStacked Stone Front Entry Design\nThis customer wanted to upgrade their home's front entry with our Kenai Stacked Stone panels and pillar panels for their front entry transformation\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/hpSnCYaA7dxNTr2ixZAJKo.jpg\" data-uuid=\"hpSnCYaA7dxNTr2ixZAJKo\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2\n\nRoger’s Home Entry Wainscoting\nLooking for inspiration to bring your home entry to life? Take a look at Roger's home entry wainscoting that uses Stratford Stacked Stone!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\nWhat Our Customers Are Saying\n\n“We used GenStone on our front entryway and couldn’t believe how fast it came together. It looks like real stone.”\n\n— Reviewer from export\n\n“The outdoor space turned out amazing. It really brought everything together.”\n\n— Reviewer from export\n\n“The install was straightforward and the finished result looks incredible.”\n\n— Reviewer from export\n\nFAQs\nAsk Away. We've Heard it All.\n\nCan GenStone be installed indoors and outdoors?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are designed for both interior and exterior applications. They are commonly used for accent walls, fireplace surrounds, entryways, garages, outdoor kitchens, and exterior facades.\n\nEvan Trevenna\n\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\nHow long does a typical GenStone project take?\n\nMost GenStone projects can be completed in a single afternoon or weekend depending on the size of the space. Because the panels are lightweight and designed to interlock, homeowners can install them much faster than traditional masonry stone.\n\nCourtney Mintz\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nDo I need special tools to install GenStone panels?\n\nNo special masonry tools are required. Most projects can be completed using common tools like a circular saw, screws, a drill, and a level. The panels are easy to cut and install using standard woodworking tools.\n\nKevin O'Dwyer\n\nGeneral Manager\n\nWhat types of projects can GenStone be used for?\n\nGenStone is commonly used for:\n\n- Accent walls\n\n- Fireplace surrounds\n\n- Garage facades\n\n- Porch columns\n\n- Entryways\n\n- Outdoor kitchens\n\n- Basement feature walls\n\nThe panels can be used anywhere you want the look of real stone without the weight or cost.\n\nRob Dean\n\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\nTrending Upgrade Areas this Month\n\nSiding Projects\n\nView Projects\n\nWainscot Projects\n\nView Projects\n\nSkirting Projects\n\nView Projects",
